{
  "id": "2026-10-01-china-mortgage-subsidy",
  "title": "Beijing starts paying part of your mortgage interest today",
  "topic": "비즈니스",
  "level": 3,
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
  "sentences": [
    "Good morning!",
    "Starting today, China is doing something it has never done before.",
    "Beijing will pay part of the interest on mortgages for first-time home buyers.",
    "The subsidy knocks one percentage point off the rate, which cuts the borrowing cost by roughly a third.",
    "It is not for everyone, though.",
    "The home has to be under 120 square meters and priced below 1.5 million yuan.",
    "The discount covers the first million yuan of the loan, for five years.",
    "That works out to about fifty thousand yuan in savings — real money, but hardly life-changing.",
    "The central government picks up ninety percent of the tab, and local governments cover the rest.",
    "What makes this unusual is not the size but the source.",
    "For the first time, central fiscal money is subsidizing interest on ordinary mortgages from commercial banks.",
    "Home prices have been falling for more than three years, and buyers have been sitting on their hands.",
    "A one-year trial is Beijing's way of asking them to stop waiting.",
    "Whether it works will say a lot about how much confidence is left in that market.",
    "Try reading those numbers out loud this morning — that is the part most of us fumble."
  ],
  "summary_ko": [
    "중국이 오늘부터 1년간 생애 첫 주택 대출 이자를 1%포인트 깎아준다 — 중앙 재정으로 상업은행 개인 대출 이자를 보조하는 건 처음이다.",
    "조건은 120㎡ 이하·150만 위안 미만 주택, 대출 100만 위안까지 5년간. 아껴지는 돈은 5만 위안 정도이고 비용은 중앙 90 · 지방 10 으로 나눈다.",
    "3년 넘게 집값이 떨어지는 동안 사람들이 더 내리길 기다리며 관망해 왔다. 이 정책의 성패가 시장에 신뢰가 얼마나 남았는지를 보여줄 것이다."
  ],
